# Build context exclusions.
#
# The context is the repository root (see apps/worker/Dockerfile's header), so without this file
# every `node_modules` in the workspace — fourteen of them, including the pnpm virtual store —
# gets uploaded to the daemon on every build. That is the difference between a context of a few
# MB and one of several hundred, on every iteration.
#
# `node_modules` is the important one for a second reason: pnpm's are trees of symlinks pointing
# at `.pnpm`, and copying them into an image produces links that resolve on the build host and
# dangle in the container. The install inside the image is what must create them, which is why
# the Dockerfile runs `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` from the lockfile rather than shipping the
# host's tree.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Rebuilt inside the image; copying it in risks shipping a `dist` from a different
# commit than the `src` beside it, which is the kind of mismatch that produces a bug nobody can
# reproduce locally.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Turbo's local cache.
.turbo
**/.turbo

# VCS and CI. `GIT_SHA` is passed as a build arg precisely so the image does not need `.git`.
.git
.github
.gitignore

# Delivery patches — these are large, are already gitignored, and have no business in an image.
*.mbox
*.patch

# Local environment and editor state.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Test and docs output that no image needs.
coverage
**/coverage
*.log
